---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Submit a candidate document" description="Suggest public-interest documents that may be worth archiving on streisandeffect.org.">
  <section class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Submission intake</p>
    <h1>Suggest a document for preservation</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Send information about documents that may be worth archiving. A submission is a lead, not approval or automatic hosting.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section callout warning">
    <h2>Email is not a secure anonymous channel</h2>
    <p>
      Ordinary email may expose your address, routing metadata, and message contents to mail providers. Submissions are not automatically confidential. Do not use this channel for private, stolen, hacked, dangerous, or highly sensitive material.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>Where to send a candidate</h2>
    <p>
      Email: <a href="mailto:submissions@streisandeffect.org">submissions@streisandeffect.org</a>
    </p>
    <p>
      Send the document title, source links, publication context, removal or alteration context, and any safety or legal concerns. Do not attach files unless the archive asks for them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>What to include</h2>
    <ul class="kicker-list">
      <li>The document title, publisher, and publication date if known.</li>
      <li>The original URL and any archived URL.</li>
      <li>Why the document appears to have been removed, hidden, altered, or made difficult to access.</li>
      <li>Why preservation is in the public interest.</li>
      <li>Relevant context, criticism, or rebuttals that should appear near the document.</li>
      <li>Whether you have a copy and how you obtained it.</li>
      <li>Any legal threats, takedown requests, public controversy, or safety concerns connected to it.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>What not to send</h2>
    <ul class="kicker-list">
      <li>Private personal information.</li>
      <li>Doxxing or material likely to create a serious safety risk.</li>
      <li>Hacked, stolen, or unlawfully obtained private material.</li>
      <li>Malware, exploit code, tracking files, or dangerous files.</li>
      <li>Large attachments unless the archive asks for them.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section metadata-panel">
    <h2>Review checklist</h2>
    <table class="meta-table">
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Public interest</th><td>Does preserving this document help accountability, research, criticism, or historical memory?</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Provenance</th><td>Can the archive identify where the document came from and whether the copy is authentic enough to present?</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Context</th><td>Can the archive explain the document without endorsing harmful or contested claims?</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Risk</th><td>Are there legal, privacy, safety, or provider-policy risks that need review before hosting?</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Retention</th><td>Submission messages may be retained while evaluating the lead and documenting any resulting archive record. A fixed retention schedule is not currently published.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
